<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gagik I of Vaspurakan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 908–943</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Gagik Artsruni</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gagik I of Vaspurakan, of the Artsruni family, was crowned king in 908 by the Sajid emir Yusuf as a rival to Smbat I of Bagratid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>. He later turned against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sajid-dynasty">Sajids</a> and became the leading Armenian ruler of his day. He built a palace and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cathedral-of-the-holy-cross-aghtamar">Church of the Holy Cross</a> on Aghtamar island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-van">Lake Van</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gagik-i-of-vaspurakan.jpg" alt="Gagik I of Vaspurakan" width="320" height="573" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francesco Bini · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Gagik_I_Artsruni_of_Vaspurakan,_%D0%90ghtamar,_facade_relief,_Armenia,_915%E2%80%93921_(portrait).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
